copilot-instructions.md instead of (or in addition to) AGENTS.md.
-->

## Persistent memory (graph-rag)

This project has an MCP-backed memory server exposing `remember`, `recall`,
and `forget` tools. Use them to keep continuity across sessions instead of
re-deriving the same context every time:

- Call **`recall(query, top_k=5)`** at the start of a task, phrasing `query`
  as a description of the task (it's a semantic search, not a keyword match).
- Call **`remember(content, kind, importance=False)`** as you learn or decide
  something worth keeping — not as an end-of-session summary. `kind` is one
  of `decision` | `correction` | `finding` | `preference` | `fact`. Set
  `importance=True` only for something that must never be pruned by decay
  even if never recalled again.
- Call **`forget(memory_id)`** immediately if a memory turns out wrong or
  superseded.

Do not save anything already derivable from the code, git history, or this
file, or anything that belongs in a commit message instead.
